+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,131 @@
+# Demand forecasting module – implementation notes
+
+Nothing could be executed in this environment (no PHP, no database), so none of this has been run. It was written
+against the existing code and checked by reading; expect to find small slips on a first real run, and run the
+checks at the end of this file.
+
+## What was built
+
+A **Forecasting** main-menu module (`modulelink` `forecast`, report link `fcst`) placed right after Manufacturing,
+with these pages (all `Forecast*.php` in the root, shared code in `includes/ForecastFunctions.php` (engine and data
+access) and `includes/ForecastFormFunctions.php` (form helpers)):
+
+| Page | Function | Page security token |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ForecastDashboard.php` | counts of active forecasts / summaries, history range, links to everything | 2 |
+| `ForecastHistory.php` | extract monthly sales history | 11 |
+| `ForecastGenerate.php` | item / category generation, best fit, batch with progress and result list | 11 |
+| `ForecastReview.php` | search, period-by-period review, revised quantities, last year's actual, variance highlight | 11 |
+| `ForecastInquiry.php` | read-only view by item, category, location, period | 2 |
+| `ForecastSummary.php` / `ForecastSummaryReview.php` | summary forecasts by category, customer type, area, salesperson, and their review screen | 11 / 2 |
+| `ForecastAccuracy.php` | MAD, POA, MSE, RMSE per item, category or method; low-accuracy flag | 2 |
+| `ForecastCompare.php` | one item, all methods side by side on a hold-out | 2 |
+| `ForecastParameters.php` | company-wide defaults | 15 (system administration) |
+| `ForecastToMRP.php` | conversion of active forecasts to MRP demands | 11 |
+
+Tokens follow the existing ones: 2 = reports/inquiries, 11 = inventory management, 15 = system administration.
+The Forecasting menu also links the existing Master Schedule (`MRPDemands.php`), MRP Calculation (`MRP.php`) and
+MRP report (`MRPReport.php`); those keep their own tokens, so the menu shows each only to roles that already had it.
+
+### Tables (all new, `forecast*`)
+`forecastparameters` (defaults), `forecasthistory` (monthly net sales by item, location, month, customer type, area,
+salesperson), `forecasts` + `forecastdetails` (item forecasts; `calcqty` and nullable `revisedqty`),
+`forecastsummaries` + `forecastsummarydetails`, `forecastbatches` + `forecastbatchitems` (batch progress and results),
+`forecastmrpdemands` (which `mrpdemands` rows the conversion wrote).
+
+One active forecast per item and location is enforced by the database: `activeflag` is 1 or NULL with a unique key
+`(stockid, loccode, activeflag)`. Generating again sets the old row's flag to NULL and inserts the new one in one
+transaction, so superseded forecasts stay on file with their method and parameters (JSON in `params`). The same
+pattern is used for summaries.
+
+## Where the sales history comes from
+
+`ForecastExtractHistory()` reads **`stockmoves`**: types 10 (sales invoice) and 11 (credit note), `hidemovt = 0`,
+quantity negated (so credits reduce sales), by `trandate` month, grouped by item and stock location, and by customer
+type (`debtorsmaster.typeid`), sales area and salesperson (`custbranch`) for the summary forecasts. These are the
+movements the stock usage report uses for sales, i.e. invoiced quantities with credits deducted, not open orders.
+(`MRPCreateDemands.php` builds on sales *orders*; the BRD says not to.) Re-running a range deletes the months in that
+range and rewrites them in one transaction. Only complete months are accepted.
+
+## How a forecast reaches MRP
+
+`ForecastToMRP.php` takes the active forecasts with periods inside a chosen date horizon (optionally one category),
+uses `COALESCE(revisedqty, calcqty)` (revised first), rounds to the item's decimal places and writes `mrpdemands`
+rows under the new demand type **`FCST`** ("Forecast (generated)"), dated the first day of the forecast month.
+The existing MRP run reads `mrpdemands` as it always did, so nothing in `MRP.php` changed (tick "use MRP demands").
+
+* Every row written is also recorded in `forecastmrpdemands` (FK to `mrpdemands.demandid`, cascade delete) with a
+  unique key on item + period. **Replace mode** deletes only recorded rows of the same items and horizon, then writes.
+  **Incremental mode** skips periods already recorded. Running either twice cannot double a demand; demands entered
+  by hand or from other sources are never touched – including hand entries that someone made under `FCST`.
+* The existing demand type `FOR` (from the 3.x upgrade) was deliberately not reused, since planners may use it by hand.
+* MRP demands have no location. If an item has an all-locations active forecast it alone is used; otherwise the
+  active forecasts of its locations are summed, so a quantity is never counted twice.
+* Note for planners: `MRP.php` also nets open sales orders; converting forecasts on top of them counts demand that is
+  both forecast and already ordered. That is standard MRP behaviour and not changed here.
+
+## Database changes (new and existing installations)
+
+* `sql/updates/44.php` – creates the tables, default parameters, demand type, `scripts` rows, the module and menu items.
+* New installs: `install/sql/tables/forecast*.sql`, `install/sql/data/{modules,forecastscripts,forecastmenuitems,forecastparameters,mrpdemandtypes}.sql`
+  (`modules.sql` regenerated with Forecasting at sequence 7 and later modules shifted), and the same rows added to
+  `install/sql/demo.sql` for the demo database. `DBUpdateNumber` on install is the highest update file, i.e. 44.
+* **Module access is positional.** `www_users.modulesallowed` is a comma list with one flag per module in `sequence`
+  order, so inserting a module in the middle would silently move every later flag. The upgrade therefore inserts a
+  `0` at position 7 of every existing user's list (existing users keep exactly their modules and do not get
+  Forecasting; the administrator grants it in User Maintenance like any other module). New users created in User
+  Maintenance default to "Yes" for every module as before. The installer's admin gets all 12 (plus the extra trailing flag it
+  always had); customer/supplier log-on setups got one more `0`.
+* `www_users.modulesallowed` was `varchar(25)`; twelve modules plus the trailing flag no longer fit, so it is widened
+  to `varchar(50)` (update and installer table).
+* `WWW_Users.php` lists the new module. Menu captions and module name are translated at display time with `__()`.
+* Translations: all new strings use `__()`; the new msgids were appended to `locale/en_GB.utf8/LC_MESSAGES/messages.pot`
+  (strings already in it were not repeated). The other `.po` files were not touched; untranslated strings fall back
+  to English until translators merge the template.
+* Install table files for older tables still say `varchar(20)` for `stockid` although update 43 widened it; that is a
+  pre-existing gap. The new tables use `varchar(64)` and carry no FK to `stockmaster`, so they work either way.
+
+## Calculation choices and BRD ambiguities
+
+* **Series.** Per item (and location): monthly net sales from the item's first month with sales to the last month of
+  held history, gaps filled with zero, negative net months counted as zero. "Months of history" is that length – an
+  item launched 8 months ago has 8, not 24. Forecast periods start the month after the last history month.
+* **History gaps.** A new extraction must overlap or abut the held range; otherwise months in between would look like
+  zero sales.
+* **Methods** (min history in brackets): 1 last year × (1+p/100) [12]; 2 last year × (sum of last 12 / sum of previous 12)
+  [24], refused if the earlier year is zero; 3 same month last year [12]; 4 flat average of last N [max(4,N)];
+  5 line through the latest month and the month k−1 earlier, k from 6 to 36 [max(6,k)]; 6 least squares [12];
+  7 quadratic least squares, refused if singular [12]; 8 flexible: user weights (not normalised, up to 12) on the latest
+  months, flat – weights summing to 1.1 give +10% [max(12,#weights)]; 9 weighted moving average, weights normalised
+  [max(4,#weights)]; 10 SES [12]; 11 Holt [12]; 12 additive Holt-Winters, initialised from the first two seasons
+  [max(24, 2×season)]. Seasonal methods 1–3 repeat the last 12 months beyond a 12-month horizon. Negative results are
+  clamped to 0. The BRD gives no formulas for 5 and 8; these are my interpretations.
+* **Smoothing constants** alpha, beta and gamma must all be 0.1–0.9 (the BRD only states it for alpha).
+* **POA.** Defined as `100 − 100·Σ|error| / Σactual`, floored at 0, "n/a" when nothing was sold. The classic
+  Σforecast/Σactual form lets over- and under-forecasts cancel, so it was not used.
+* **Best fit.** Last *H* months held out (default 3), every method with enough history left is run, lowest MAD wins
+  (item). For a category, methods are compared on summed absolute error ÷ summed actuals over the items they could be
+  tested on, considering only methods testable on at least half the testable items; the winner is applied to all items
+  of the category, and items it cannot handle fail with the reason rather than silently using another method.
+* **Category scope** = items with `discontinued = 0` and not service/dummy (`mbflag <> 'D'`). Items without history
+  fail with a reason.
+* **Batches** run 25 items per request and continue automatically (and resumably) until done. The category best-fit
+  test runs once when the batch is created.
+* **Accuracy** compares every forecast period that already has history (superseded forecasts included unless "active
+  only" is ticked) using the effective quantity (revised first). Items are grouped by item+location.
+* **Summary forecasts** are calculated from the aggregated history of the group, not as a sum of item forecasts; the
+  review screen shows the history, the biggest contributing items and, for categories, the sum of active item forecasts
+  next to the summary. Summaries cannot be revised (the BRD only asks for revisions on item forecasts) and are not sent
+  to MRP.
+* **Variance** is `(quantity used − last year actual) / last year actual`; highlighted at ±25% by default (editable on the
+  page); shown as "-" when last year is outside the held history or zero.
+* **Locations.** History and forecasts are company-wide data; the location pickers and the review/inquiry/accuracy
+  pages respect the user's location view permissions (all-locations forecasts are visible to everyone with the page token).
+* Out of scope per the BRD and not built: email/cron automation, promotions, value forecasts, what-if.
+
+## Checks to run first
+1. Apply the upgrade on a copy of a database that has users; confirm each user's `modulesallowed` gained a `0` at position 7
+   and that menus and permissions are unchanged, then grant Forecasting to a test user.
+2. Fresh install (with and without demo data) and confirm the Forecasting tab, menu entries and `FCST` demand type.
+3. Extract 24 months, generate for an item and a small category, revise a quantity, convert twice in each mode and
+   confirm `mrpdemands` is not doubled and manual demands remain.
